auth: separate finance.manage from finance.view

Recording an expense and setting a food cost target both checked
staffCan("finance.view") — a permission src/domain/permissions.ts documents
as "Read only", the payments ledger.

The conflation had a visible consequence. ADMIN is deliberately excluded
from finance.view, because the ledger is "OWNER and MANAGER only, the
people who run the till day to day". That read decision was also deciding
who could write, so the result came out upside down: an ADMIN could not
record an expense while a MANAGER could, despite ADMIN holding
orders.refund, menu.price, staff.manage and audit.view.

finance.manage now gates the two writes and the three UI controls that
offer them. Server check and UI gate moved together — a button that renders
and then fails on submit is its own bug.

Nobody's access changed. finance.manage is granted to OWNER and MANAGER,
exactly the roles that could write before, and a test asserts that role by
role. ADMIN is excluded by an explicit line rather than by the filter
default, because ADMIN is "everything except settings.manage and
finance.view" — so letting a new permission fall through would have handed
it the ability to write into the P&L as a side effect of a refactor.

Whether ADMIN should be able to record an expense is a real question and
not one to answer from the code. Recorded in PENDING-DECISIONS.md with the
one-line fix if the answer is yes.

462 tests (from 459), typecheck, lint and the RSC-boundary check all clean.

